diff --git a/NOTES.md b/NOTES.md
index 3c8f9f8..572909c 100644
--- a/NOTES.md
+++ b/NOTES.md
@@ -36,10 +36,10 @@ Taixin TXW8301 (TXW4002A, C-SKY CK803) HaLow wireless-bridge (WNB) firmware SDK
 - Writes are staged, validated, committed, and applied after the response is sent (`webui_run_todo`). To add a setting, add it to `webui_get_value()` and `webui_set_value()`. Read-only status keys: `fwver`, `buildtime` (`__DATE__ __TIME__` of `webui.c`, which `prebuild.sh` forces to recompile on every build), `uptime`, `s_ipaddr`/`s_netmask`/`s_gw_ip` (live w0), `heap_free`/`heap_total` (`sram_heap`), `skb_free`/`skb_total` (WiFi packet-buffer pool), all in bytes; `pair_state` (bit0 started from the web and not stopped, kept in `webui.c`; bit1 `sys_status.pair_success`, set by `events.c`).
 - WiFi key: an empty `sys_cfgs.passwd` means the raw `psk` is the key (set by `wifi_passwd=<64 hex>`, `AT+PSK`, or a successful pairing on a station, which all clear `passwd`). Then `wifi_passwd=?` returns the PSK as 64 hex digits, and an SSID change keeps the key instead of re-deriving it (as the vendor `AT+SSID` does). A passphrase is limited to 32 characters by `passwd[PASSWD_MAX_LEN+1]`.
 - Default web password is `admin` (`WEBUI_DEFAULT_PASSWD`), stored in the `webcfg` region.
-- UI source: `../hgic-wnb-web-master` (Vue 3 + Vite, modified from the vendor's version). Its `AGENTS.md` is outdated: vue-i18n, vue-router and @vicons/utils were replaced by small stand-ins in `src/lite/`, mapped through aliases in `vite.config.ts` **and** `tsconfig.json`. The UI is English-only; a Vite plugin keeps only `enUS` from each SFC `<i18n>` block.
+- UI source: `../web` in the taixin-halow-bridge repo (Vue 3 + Vite, modified from the vendor's version). Its `AGENTS.md` is outdated: vue-i18n, vue-router and @vicons/utils were replaced by small stand-ins in `src/lite/`, mapped through aliases in `vite.config.ts` **and** `tsconfig.json`. The UI is English-only; a Vite plugin keeps only `enUS` from each SFC `<i18n>` block.
 - The stand-ins support only what the UI uses today (named routes, `t('key')` with no interpolation). Extend them rather than re-adding the real libraries.
 - After any UI change:
-  1. `npm run build` in `../hgic-wnb-web-master` (runs `vue-tsc`).
+  1. `npm run build` in `../web` (runs `vue-tsc`).
   2. `powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File project\utilities\gen_webui_page.ps1` (regenerates `project/webui_page.h`; `-Placeholder` writes a stub page).
   3. Rebuild the firmware.
   4. Check the gzip size reported by step 2. It is ~53 KB now; it costs the same amount of SRAM and counts against the OTA limit.
